<?xml version="1.0" standalone="yes"?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
<!ENTITY name "dedupe">
<!ENTITY author "James Green">
<!ENTITY version "2026.10.31">
<!ENTITY pluginURL "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/greenycq20/unraid-dedupe/main/dedupe.plg">
]>
<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" pluginURL="&pluginURL;" min="6.9.0" icon="clone">

<CHANGES>
###2026.10.31
- FEATURE: Added Smart "Keep" Selection strategies:
  * Keep Oldest (preserves earliest modified file, marks newer copies for deletion)
  * Keep Newest (preserves most recently modified file)
  * Keep Shortest Path (preserves cleanest/shortest path)
  * Keep by Preferred Path Pattern (prioritize keeping files in specific shares/directories)
- FEATURE: File Extension Filtering (Include specific extensions like mkv, mp4, iso; or Exclude extensions like nfo, srt, tmp).
- FEATURE: CSV Report Export (download full duplicate audit report directly to CSV).
- FEATURE: Automated Scheduled Scans (Disabled, Daily, Weekly, Monthly) via Unraid cron with native notification alerts.
- FEATURE: Enhanced Deletion Preview modal with detailed breakdown of files and space to be reclaimed.
- IMPROVEMENT: Added file modification dates and timestamps to duplicate results table.
- IMPROVEMENT: Added log rotation (caps log at 1MB / last 1000 lines to prevent RAM exhaustion).
- IMPROVEMENT: Configuration persistence in /boot/config/plugins/dedupe/dedupe.cfg across reboots.

###2026.10.30
- SECURITY: Fixed XSS vulnerability — all file paths are now escaped before rendering in the results table.
- SECURITY: Fixed path traversal in delete API — uses realpath() to canonicalize paths before validation.
- SECURITY: Fixed potential command injection via PID file — PIDs are now validated as numeric.
- SECURITY: Added Content-Type headers to all JSON API responses.
- FIX: Implemented deep verification (byte-by-byte cmp) — previously the checkbox was accepted but never used.
- FIX: Scan script now handles empty directories and zero-candidate scenarios gracefully.
- FIX: Progress calculation no longer divides by zero when no candidates are found.
- FIX: Status file writes are now atomic (write to temp, then mv) to prevent corrupt JSON reads.
- FIX: Removed broken PNG icon placeholder; plugin now uses FontAwesome icon exclusively.
- FIX: Page-load status check now handles 'idle' state properly and doesn't start polling.
- FIX: Added AJAX error handlers to all API calls for user feedback on failures.
- IMPROVEMENT: Added minimum file size filter to skip tiny files.
- IMPROVEMENT: Added exclusion pattern support (.Recycle.Bin, @eaDir, thumbs, etc).
- IMPROVEMENT: Results persist across page navigation — reload the page and results are still there.
- IMPROVEMENT: Better delete confirmation showing file count and estimated space reclamation.
- IMPROVEMENT: Scan log now shows file counts, timing, and space statistics.

###2026.04.01
- CRITICAL FIX: Hardcoded plugin name in uninstallation bash script to prevent XML CDATA variable escaping which caused the entire plugins RAM directory to be wiped.
- Fixed uninstallation cleanup to ensure the tool is removed from the webGUI immediately.
- Restored full SHA hash suite (SHA-1, SHA-224, SHA-256, SHA-384, SHA-512).
- Generalized all comments and UI text for public release.
- Unified plugin icons and added description for the Plugins page.
- Integrated Unraid Native Notification system for scan completion alerts.
- Added space reclamation tracking: logs now show total space saved after deletions.
</CHANGES>

<DESCRIPTION>
A high-performance deduplication tool for Unraid. Scan your shares for identical files using hardware-accelerated SHA/MD5 hashing and reclaim wasted array space with ease.
</DESCRIPTION>

